A div is an ordinary container, not inert template storage. Its descendants enter the document immediately. Supplied JavaScript bridge (execute separately with the original TEMPLATE worked example, not the changed DIV example, in a supported DOM host):
```javascript
const template = document.querySelector("#card-template");
const copy = template.content.cloneNode(true);
