after:
This optional JavaScript uses the same template. It is a preview of the DOM lessons in the JavaScript course.

```javascript
const template = document.querySelector("#card-template");
const copy = template.content.cloneNode(true);
document.querySelector("#cards").append(copy);
```

The first line finds the template. `content` holds its stored nodes—the HTML pieces. `cloneNode(true)` copies those pieces and everything inside them. `append(copy)` puts the copied pieces into the section. The original template stays available.
